From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v0lumehi <aljic.zijad@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:28:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] iOS: touch keys that toggle (DM_TOUCH_TOGGLE)

Holding a touch key for a long time is tiring, for example to run or to
accelerate. The shell's touch layout editor now sets each key to Hold or
Toggle and passes the toggled ones as DM_TOUCH_TOGGLE, control names joined
by commas (zl,zr,a). A tap on such a key turns it on, the next tap off, and
the key is drawn pressed while it is on. Only single keys toggle: the
diamond as a whole, the left stick and the D-pad are skipped, so is an
unknown name. Opening the in-game menu, a pose change, a connected
controller and the controller prompt release a toggled key with every
other key, so nothing stays on behind a menu.

dm_pad_toggle_parse in DmPadGeometry.h reads the value, DmGamepad.m keeps
the keys that are on and adds them to the pressed buttons.

Tests: pad_geometry_check.m (the value's form, skipped names, the limit),
test_env_switches.py (the new row).

Upstream-Status: pending [builds on the touch patches 0065 to 0070 and 0090, forwarded once those land upstream]
Reason: Touch keys that toggle, set per key in the shell's touch layout editor
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#658
